# These barrels are append-only `export *`/re-export manifests: concurrent
# PRs that each add a new module or symbol only conflict here because git's
# default 3-way merge treats adjacent-line insertions as competing hunks,
# even though "keep both lines" is always the correct resolution for an
# unordered export list. `merge=union` is git's built-in driver for exactly
# this — on a conflicting hunk it takes both sides instead of writing
# conflict markers.
#
# Scope this to barrel files ONLY. Any file with real logic must never have
# both sides of a conflict silently kept — see
# packages/fractal/src/barrel-lines.test.ts, which guards against the one
# failure mode union merge introduces (both sides adding the identical line).
packages/fractal/src/index.ts merge=union
packages/fractal/src/domain/index.ts merge=union
packages/fractal/src/ports/index.ts merge=union
packages/fractal/src/fakes/index.ts merge=union
